<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="api_irtcengine_getcallid">
    <title><ph keyref="getCallId"/></title>
    <shortdesc id="short"><ph id="shortdesc" props="cpp">Gets the current call ID.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="android">Gets the current call ID.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="ios mac">Retrieves the call ID.</ph></shortdesc>
    <prolog>
        <metadata>
            <keywords>
                <indexterm keyref="getCallId"/>
            </keywords>
        </metadata>
    </prolog>
    <refbody>
        <section id="prototype">
            <p outputclass="codeblock">
                <codeblock props="cpp" outputclass="language-cpp">virtual int getCallId(agora::util::AString&amp; callId) = 0;</codeblock>
                <codeblock props="android" outputclass="language-java">public abstract String getCallId();</codeblock>
            <codeblock props="ios mac" outputclass="language-objectivec">- (NSString * _Nullable)getCallId;</codeblock>
            <codeblock props="ios" outputclass="language-objectivec">- (NSString * _Nullable)getCallId NS_SWIFT_NAME(getCallId());</codeblock>
                </p>
        </section>
        <section id="detailed_desc" deliveryTarget="details" otherprops="no-title">
            <p props="cpp">When a user joins a channel on the client, the SDK generates a <codeph>callId</codeph> to identify the call. You can call this method to get the <codeph>callId</codeph> and pass it to methods such as <xref keyref="rate"/> and <xref keyref="complain"/>.</p>
            <p props="android">After the user joins a channel, the client generates a <codeph>callId</codeph> to identify the current call. You can call <xref keyref="getCallId"/> to get the <codeph>callId</codeph>, and pass it when calling methods such as <xref keyref="rate"/> and <xref keyref="complain"/>.</p>
        <p id="detail" props="ios mac">When a user joins a channel on a client, a <parmname>callId</parmname> is generated to identify the call from the client. <ph props="android cpp apple framework">You can call this method to get <parmname>callId</parmname>, and pass it in when calling methods such as <xref keyref="rate"/> and <xref keyref="complain"/>.</ph></p>
            </section>
        <section id="timing" deliveryTarget="details" props="android cpp">
            <title>Timing</title>
            <p props="cpp">Call this method after joining a channel.</p>
            <p props="android">You must call this method after joining a channel.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="parameters" deliveryTarget="details" props="cpp ios mac">
            <title>Parameters</title>
            <parml>
                <plentry props="cpp">
                    <pt>callId</pt>
                    <pd>Output parameter. The <codeph>callId</codeph> of the current call.</pd>
                </plentry>
            <plentry id="callid" props="ios mac">
                    <pt>callId</pt>
                    <pd>Output parameter, the current call ID.</pd>
                </plentry>
            </parml>
        </section>
        <section id="return_values" props="android cpp ios mac">
            <title>Return Values</title>
            <p props="cpp">
                <ul>
                    <li>0: Success.</li>
                    <li>&lt; 0: Failure.</li>
                </ul>
            </p>
            <p props="android">
                <ul>
                    <li>If the method call succeeds, returns the current call <codeph>callId</codeph>.</li>
                    <li>If the method call fails, returns an empty string.</li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        <p props="ios mac">The current call ID.</p>
            </section>
    </refbody>
</reference>
